.TH SYNAPSED 1 "2026" "synapseids" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
synapsed \- SynapseIDS capture, flow, feature and inference daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B synapsed
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-\-listen\fR \fIhost:port\fR]
[\fB\-\-capture\fR \fIiface\fR]
.br
.B synapsed \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B synapsed
manages capture sources, decodes packets, builds bidirectional flows, extracts
the frozen
.I flow-features-v1
vector for each flow, scores it with one or more inference models, persists the
results, and exposes a versioned REST API together with a single live WebSocket
channel.
.PP
A replayed capture runs through exactly the same flow, feature and
classification pipeline as live traffic, so the UI behaves identically. Live
local\-interface capture is wired via
.BR \-\-capture ;
tcpdump\-stream, SSH and PCAP\-over\-IP backends and trained ONNX models arrive in
later releases.
.PP
The management API binds to
.B 127.0.0.1:8080
by default. Binding it to a non\-loopback address is logged as a warning; put an
authenticating reverse proxy in front for remote access.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Load configuration from a JSON file. See
.B contrib/config/synapse.json
for an annotated example. Environment variables
.RB ( SYNAPSE_LISTEN ", " SYNAPSE_STORAGE_DRIVER ", " SYNAPSE_MODELS_DIR ", ...)
override file values.
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " host:port"
Override
.B server.listen
from the command line.
.TP
.BI \-\-capture " iface"
Capture live traffic from a local network interface via
.BR AF_PACKET .
Repeatable. Adds a promiscuous NIC source equivalent to a
.B capture.sources
entry; the environment variable
.B SYNAPSE_CAPTURE_IFACE
does the same. Requires
.B CAP_NET_RAW
(and
.B CAP_NET_ADMIN
for promiscuous mode); running as root is not required. A source that cannot
open is logged and skipped, and the API keeps serving.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print build metadata and exit.
.SH ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/status
Daemon, storage, event\-bus, live\-channel and replay status.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/flows \fR/\fB /api/v1/flows/{id}
Recent flow records; one flow with its raw feature vector.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/classifications
Recent ensemble verdicts (the rolling log feed).
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/captures \fR/\fB /api/v1/captures/{name}
Live capture sources: state, packets/sec, bytes/sec, kernel drops, filter.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/schemas/features \fR/\fB /api/v1/schemas/classes
The frozen feature and output contracts.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/replay
Start a PCAP replay: JSON body
.RB { \(dqpath\(dq ,\  \(dqspeed\(dq }.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/stream
WebSocket channel of batched event envelopes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/synapseids/synapse.json
Recommended configuration path (see contrib/).
.TP
.B /var/lib/synapseids
Recommended state directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
clean shutdown;
.B 1
configuration or server error;
.B 2
usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR synapse (1),
.BR synapse-sensor (1),
.BR tcpdump (1),
.BR editcap (1)
